<title>POLAND: BAYER VB TO ISSUE PLN 100 MLN POLISH BONDS.</title>
<headline>BAYER VB TO ISSUE PLN 100 MLN POLISH BONDS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Bayerische Vereinsbank AG will issue straight fixed two-year bonds in Poland worth 100 million zlotys, a banking source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The source, which asked not to be named, said the bonds would carry an annual coupon of 16 percent. The source said the issue would be jointly managed by Polish Pekao SA bank and the Polish unit of Vereinsbank, Vereinsbank-Polska SA.</p>
<p>The banks' officials were not immediately available to confirm the report or give more details.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
